joint linked systems of quartet trees. We refer to these systems as \emph{meshed systems} and use them to show that any set of quartets of sufficient size is decisive. 

\begin{defn}
A \emph{meshed system} on a tree $T$ with taxon set $X$ is an $(n-3)$ by $(n-3)$ array of quartet trees, where each row is a linked system and each column is a vine.
\end{defn}

